# Spotify Web API conventions (this repo)

## Documentation sources (prefer in order)

1. **Official llms.txt** — https://developer.spotify.com/llms.txt
2. **OpenAPI spec** — https://developer.spotify.com/reference/web-api/open-api-schema.yaml
3. **Building with AI** — https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api/tutorials/building-with-ai
4. **Context7 MCP** — `get-library-docs` with `/websites/developer_spotify_web-api` (see `AGENTS.md`)

Do not guess endpoint paths or JSON field names — use the OpenAPI spec.

## Project-specific rules

- **Server-only**: Spotify client ID/secret, tokens, and `spotifyFetch()` stay in `src/lib/server/**` or `+server.ts`. Never expose secrets or access tokens to the browser.
- **OAuth flow**: Authorization Code (backend) in `src/lib/server/auth/spotify-oauth.ts` — not PKCE, not Client Credentials for user data, not Implicit Grant (deprecated).
- **Scopes**: request only what the app needs (`playlist-read-private`, `playlist-read-collaborative`, `user-top-read`, `user-follow-read`). Add new scopes in `spotify-oauth.ts` and README together.
- **Tokens**: store in encrypted session cookie via `jose`; refresh with `refreshAccessToken()` before expiry (`ensureFreshSession()` in `client.ts`).
- **API client**: use `spotifyFetch(session, path)` — paths are relative to `https://api.spotify.com/v1`.
- **Types**: minimal interfaces in `src/lib/types/spotify.ts`; align shapes with OpenAPI schemas.
- **Rate limits**: on HTTP 429, respect `Retry-After`; use exponential backoff — do not tight-loop retries.
- **Compliance**: follow [Developer Terms](https://developer.spotify.com/terms); cache only what immediate use requires.

## Modules

| Module | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `src/lib/server/auth/spotify-oauth.ts` | Authorize URL, code exchange, token refresh |
| `src/lib/server/auth/session.ts` | Encrypted session cookie |
| `src/lib/server/spotify/client.ts` | `spotifyFetch`, `ensureFreshSession`, `/me` |
| `src/lib/server/spotify/playlists.ts` | User playlists |
| `src/lib/server/spotify/artists.ts` | Top/followed/playlist artists |

## Redirect URI

- Local dev: `http://localhost:5173/auth/callback` (configured in README; register in Spotify Dashboard)
- Production: HTTPS callback on your Vercel domain
- Spotify allows `http://127.0.0.1` for local dev per their redirect URI guide; this project uses `localhost` — keep Dashboard URIs in sync with `SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI`.
